From: lws-hmi <dev@lws>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 10:50:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] compositor: clamp HW cursor to display size

user_input tracks the pointer in display (DRM/scanout) coordinates and
passes display-space deltas to compositor_set_cursor. The KMS cursor
plane also places the icon in display coordinates.

Clamping to view_size is wrong under -o landscape_*/portrait_* when
view_size is the swapped Flutter logical size (e.g. 1280x800) while
display_size remains the panel mode (e.g. 800x1280). That makes the
visible pointer travel a rectangle that does not match the screen.

Clamp to display_size (0 .. w-1, 0 .. h-1) to match user_input.
---
--- a/src/compositor_ng.c
+++ b/src/compositor_ng.c
@@ -556,16 +556,18 @@
 
         struct view_geometry viewgeo = window_get_view_geometry(compositor->main_window);
 
+        /* Deltas and DRM cursor placement are in display coordinates; do not
+         * clamp to view_size (swapped under rotation). Match user_input. */
         if (compositor->cursor_pos.x < 0.0f) {
             compositor->cursor_pos.x = 0.0f;
-        } else if (compositor->cursor_pos.x > viewgeo.view_size.x) {
-            compositor->cursor_pos.x = viewgeo.view_size.x;
+        } else if (compositor->cursor_pos.x > viewgeo.display_size.x - 1.0f) {
+            compositor->cursor_pos.x = viewgeo.display_size.x - 1.0f;
         }
 
         if (compositor->cursor_pos.y < 0.0f) {
             compositor->cursor_pos.y = 0.0f;
-        } else if (compositor->cursor_pos.y > viewgeo.view_size.y) {
-            compositor->cursor_pos.y = viewgeo.view_size.y;
+        } else if (compositor->cursor_pos.y > viewgeo.display_size.y - 1.0f) {
+            compositor->cursor_pos.y = viewgeo.display_size.y - 1.0f;
         }
     }
 
